164: 1  INTRODUCTION
165: 
166: 1.1  Aims and objectives
167: 
168: The WJEC Eduqas GCSE in Food Preparation and Nutrition equips learners with the
169: knowledge, understanding and skills required to cook and apply the principles of food
170: science, nutrition and healthy eating. It encourages learners to cook, enables them to
171: make informed decisions about food and nutrition and allows them to acquire
172: knowledge in order to be able to feed themselves and others affordably and
173: nutritiously, now and later in life.
174: 
175: This specification has been designed to enable centres to concentrate on innovative
176: delivery of the course whilst creating a balance between practical and theoretical
177: knowledge and understanding. The layout of the content into six areas of content
178: promotes flexibility of delivery, and releasing two tasks for each of the assessments
179: that constitute the non-examination assessment will ensure learners are able to
180: complete assessments suitable to their needs and that of the centre.

